			<div class="content" id="post-content-2345092">
									

<p><a href="https://wordcounter.net">Word count</a> is: 500</p>
<p>As proof:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-2312/Screen%20Shot%202015-07-25%20at%2009.46.57%20.png" alt="Screen%20Shot%202015-07-25%20at%2009.46.57%20.png" class="image" />
<hr />
<img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-2312/Screen%20Shot%202015-07-25%20at%2009.47.13%20.png" alt="Screen%20Shot%202015-07-25%20at%2009.47.13%20.png" class="image" /></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Firstly, I would like to thank Ms. Light and other contest organisers for bringing this lovely contest to the site. This has been a fun and engaging experience for me. And I have used every single word I can get away with.</p>
<p>Secondly, I would like to thank the many people who had reviewed this draft such as azzleflux, Decibelles, OZ Ouroborus etc. (there were too many whom I showed to).</p>
<p>Special thanks to psul for his review, his faith in this article and bothering to check the word count on his initiative even when he was checking out another article.</p>
<p>Lastly, I would like to thank my patience for waiting for another day to post this since I made a last minute change that I feel is for the best and justifies this short article here.</p>
<p>The image is credited to Abser of Wikipedia (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:TRNC_location.png">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:TRNC_location.png</a>) via CC BY-SA 3.0.</p>
<p>Date format used here is dd/mm/yyyy.</p>
<p>Since I do this for all my articles, what's going on?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>King Pan, in summary, is a multiversal feudal king that controls multiple dimensions' iterations of &quot;Cyprus&quot;. Since he is based in the Kyrenias as his &quot;capital&quot;, it is established as the link to all other dimensions' Cyprus. i.e. King Pan controls a state that currently has the Kyrenias as part of its territory.</p>
<p>The benefactor is actually Saturn Deer, a character crafted by Dmatix. Go search the site for his Saturn Deer works and support them too.</p>
<p>If you take note of the dates, the update was made after the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypriot_Annan_Plan_referendums,_2004">Annam Plan</a>. And <strong>no</strong>, the Foundation have no part in the outcome. I mean, the Annam Plan is manned by the UN (parent organisation of their no. 1 rival – GOC). Besides, the Foundation is an organisation of mostly R&amp;D, intelligence and military elements. Diplomats would not be their strong point.</p>
<p>Anyway, the status of Cyprus may be purely of the people's will or something else?</p>
<p>As for the shortness, it is implied to be from lower clearance level (Level 2, in fact). The information presented here are solely on a need-to-know basis, enough for the in-universe reader to fulfil his job scope.</p>
</div>
</div>
